---
// Category shelf: an editorial header row (heading left, intro right) over a
// plain two-to-four-column text list of the eight categories. No cards, no
// tiles: the list is bare text, and no spacing depends on whitespace between
// inline elements (Astro strips those, which ran words together before).
---

<section class="categories" id="categories" aria-labelledby="categories-heading">
  <div class="cat-head reveal">
    <h2 id="categories-heading">Start with a category</h2>
    <p class="cat-intro">
      Whatever you are shopping for, you can go straight to it. The market is
      sorted into eight categories, each stocked by trusted sellers across
      Malawi.
    </p>
  </div>

  
</section>

<style>
  .categories {
    padding: clamp(2.25rem, 6vw, 4rem) 0;
  }

  .cat-head {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.25rem;
  }

  .cat-head h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 2.6vw, 1.875rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.15;
  }

  .cat-intro {
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--body);
    max-width: 56ch;
  }

  /* Desktop: heading and intro share one row, intro slightly wider so the
     heading never squeezes it. */
  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .cat-head {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.9fr) minmax(0, 1.1fr);
      gap: 3rem;
      align-items: start;
    }
  }

  .cat-list {
    margin: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 2.5rem) 0 0;
    padding: clamp(1.25rem, 3vw, 1.75rem) 0 0;
    border-top: 1px solid #D8DEE9;
    list-style: none;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 0.875rem 1.5rem;
  }

  .cat-list li {
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--navy);
  }

  /* Four across on desktop: the eight categories read as two tidy rows. */
  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .cat-list {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }
</style>
